
# --- natural-language query layer (spec 5.2) -- entirely optional ---
#
# With no key the command palette still resolves phrases against its own lookup
# table, which is the deterministic fallback 5.2 requires. Setting a key only
# adds interpretation of phrasing the table cannot parse.
#
# Any OpenAI-compatible endpoint works. OpenRouter for the demo; point
# NLQ_BASE_URL at http://127.0.0.1:11434/v1 for a local Ollama server and the
# key becomes unnecessary -- which is the self-hosted path 5.2 says production
# would take, since a ministry would not route operational queries through a
# third-party API.
#
# Free-tier caveat worth stating out loud in the pitch: free OpenRouter models
# generally log prompts and rate-limit aggressively. Only the catalogue's
# vocabulary is ever sent -- variable names, region ids, timestep strings,
# float numbers -- never measurements and never anything about who is running it.
OCEANUPS_NLQ_API_KEY=
OCEANUPS_NLQ_MODEL=nvidia/nemotron-3.5-lightning:free
OCEANUPS_NLQ_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
